   ],
   "text": "LOSS OF LIFE FOLLOWING MAN OVERBOARD FROM P/V QUEEN OF THE WEST",
   "conf": 0.9913,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    86.2,
    66.5,
    532.6,
    78.5
   ],
   "text": "27. The rescue boat had a compartment labeled \"Searchlight\" but did not have a searchlight onboard.",
   "conf": 0.9911,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    152.9,
    76.9,
    517.1,
    91.6
   ],
   "text": "ran from the Main Deck to the 4th Deck Bridge to obtain flashlights for the rescue",
   "conf": 0.9816,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    103.3,
    78.5,
    123.5,
    90.8
   ],
   "text": "Mr.",
   "conf": 0.9973,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    102.9,
    90.4,
    253.8,
    103.5
   ],
   "text": "boat crew to use while searching.",
   "conf": 0.9965,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    86.2,
    114.7,
    320.1,
    126.6
   ],
   "text": "28. At about 0110 hrs, the rescue boat was launched.",
   "conf": 0.9824,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    85.8,
    138.6,
    195.0,
    150.5
   ],
   "text": "29. At 0111 hrs Captain",
   "conf": 0.9817,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    243.1,
    138.6,
    523.1,
    150.5
   ],
   "text": "contacted the Coast Guard via VHF Ch. 16 and then called 911",
   "conf": 0.998,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    102.5,
    150.5,
    168.0,
    164.1
   ],
   "text": "by cell phone.",
   "conf": 0.9994,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    85.4,
    174.0,
    457.2,
    187.6
   ],
   "text": "30. At 0116 hrs a Fire and Rescue Truck arrived and began searching the shore line.",
   "conf": 0.9977,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    85.4,
    199.1,
    515.9,
    211.1
   ],
   "text": "31. At 0204 hrs, the Coast Guard helicopter CG 6035 arrived on-scene and began its search. The",
   "conf": 0.9931,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    103.3,
    211.1,
    499.7,
    223.0
   ],
   "text": "Coast Guard helicopter requested the crew throw a lighted life ring in the water for datum",
   "conf": 0.9855,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    280.4,
    223.0,
    527.5,
    235.0
   ],
   "text": "threw a lighted life ring in the water. This was the first",
   "conf": 0.9943,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    103.7,
    223.4,
    233.5,
    235.4
   ],
   "text": "collection purposes. Captain",
   "conf": 0.9899,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    103.3,
    235.4,
    394.8,
    247.3
   ],
   "text": "buoyant object to enter the water since Mr. Staples fell overboard.",
   "conf": 0.9982,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    85.4,
    259.2,
    500.5,
    270.8
   ],
   "text": "32. At 0235 hrs, the vessel's crew recovered the rescue boat. The rescue boat crew found Mr.",
   "conf": 0.9906,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    103.3,
    271.6,
    279.2,
    283.5
   ],
   "text": "Staples'tan jacket floating in the water.",
   "conf": 0.9919,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    84.6,
    295.1,
    197.8,
    308.2
   ],
   "text": "33. At 0400 hrs, Captain",
   "conf": 0.9824,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    244.7,
    295.5,
    531.8,
    307.4
   ],
   "text": "conducted alcohol breathalyzer testing for the six crew members",
   "conf": 0.9829,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    102.5,
    306.6,
    349.9,
    320.2
   ],
   "text": "directly involved. All results were negative for alcohol.",
   "conf": 0.996,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    83.8,
    330.1,
    508.8,
    345.3
   ],
   "text": "34. P/V QUEEN OF THE WEST departed from Rainier, OR at 0454 hrs to continue its voyage.",
   "conf": 0.9953,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    83.8,
    354.4,
    533.0,
    368.4
   ],
   "text": "35. On 08AUG12 at 1130 hrs, the three witnesses present when Mr. Staples fell overboard were drug",
   "conf": 0.9899,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    102.1,
    368.0,
    523.1,
    379.9
   ],
   "text": "tested at Hood River, OR. All drug tests were later confirmed \"negative\" by a Medical Review",
   "conf": 0.9926,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    101.7,
    379.1,
    139.4,
    391.9
   ],
   "text": "Officer.",
   "conf": 0.9999,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    83.4,
    402.6,
    521.5,
    416.1
   ],
   "text": "36. On 12AUG12 at 0624 hrs, two civilian boaters found Mr. Staples' body in the Columbia River",
   "conf": 0.9909,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    101.7,
    415.3,
    521.1,
    428.5
   ],
   "text": "channel in approximate position 46-11.3N 123-08.63W, 11 NM northwest of where he entered",
   "conf": 0.9965,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    100.9,
    427.3,
    147.0,
    439.2
   ],
   "text": "the water.",
   "conf": 0.9636,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    83.4,
    450.8,
    280.8,
    464.3
   ],
   "text": "37. On 09NOV12, Cowlitz County Coroner",
   "conf": 0.9975,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    340.0,
    452.0,
    531.8,
    463.9
   ],
   "text": "indicated that Mr. Staples died of asphyxia",
   "conf": 0.9992,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    101.7,
    463.9,
    526.3,
    475.9
   ],
   "text": "by drowning. His death was ruled as an accident. Toxicology specimens were unattainable due",
   "conf": 0.9995,
   "retry": null
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    101.7,
    475.9,
    409.5,
    487.8
   ],
